\(\min.\left\{Q_{S}^{A},Q_{S}^{B}\right\}\), where \(Q_{S}^{A}\) and \(Q_{S}^{B}\) are respectively the saturation scales of the two colliding protons at that \(x_{\perp}\). This choice is motivated by the fact that the inclusive multiplicity of produced gluons is much more sensitive to the smaller of the two saturation scales [260]. In Fig. 4.17 (left) we plot the saturation scale as a function of \(\sqrt{s}\) for different impact parameters. The right plot has on the \(y\)-axis the quantity that appears in Eq. 4.28 determined by the procedure we described. We observe that a stronger dependence of this quantity is seen for the b-CGC model. With the exception of the parameter \(\zeta\), we have everything necessary to compute Eq. 4.27 at a given impact parameter.

