### 4.6 Particle production : Non-perturbative approach

In this section we discuss the computation of multiplicity in a non-perturbative approach by combining the IP-Sat (Impact Parameter Saturation Model) model [266, 267] of high energy nucleon (and nuclear) wavefunctions with the classical Yang-Mills (CYM) dynamics of the Glasma fields produced after the heavy-ion collision [268, 269, 270, 272, 274, 275]. We call this newly developed framework as the IP-Glasma (Impact Parameter Dependent Glasma) model. A detailed description of the IP-Glasma model can be found in [276, 277, 278]. Parameters of IP-Glasma model are constrained by global fits to the HERA data.

